<title>HONG KONG: China's Zhejiang Expressway offers H-shares.</title>
<headline>China's Zhejiang Expressway offers H-shares.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's state-owned Zhejiang Expressway Co Ltd is offering 1.25 billion H-shares at HK$2.06-2.38 each, it said in a statement published on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The offer comprises a placement and an initial public offering (IPO), it said. But it did not elaborate.</p>
<p>Dealings in the H shares, or Chinese state-owned enterprises listed in Hong Kong, are expected to start on May 15.</p>
<p>The IPO runs from Tuesday to Friday, the statement said.</p>
<p>The issue price per share is not more than HK$2.38 and expected to be not less than HK$2.06, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
